Overview
This directory contains the GHDL simulation environment for the module:

cmd_parser_slave_generic

It provides a standalone testbench for validating the parser together with the generic slave model, using GHDL and GTKWave.

This README focuses only on how to run the simulation.
For parser architecture, command format, and slave behavior, please refer to the main project documentation.

Directory Structure
File / Directory	Description
Makefile	Automation for compile, elaborate, run, and waveform visualization
cmd.txt	Command sequence executed by the parser
ram_init.cde	Initial RAM contents for the generic slave
workdir/	GHDL working directory (object files, elaboration artifacts)
wave.ghw / wave.vcd / wave.fst	Waveform output (format depends on Makefile settings)
README.md	This document


Requirements
GHDL (LLVM or mcode backend recommended)

GTKWave (for waveform visualization)

MSYS2 / MINGW64 or Linux shell environment

Standard VHDL‑93 support (used by the Makefile)

Makefile Overview
The Makefile supports:

multiple VHDL standards (93, 93c, 2002, 2008)

selectable waveform formats (ghw, vcd, fst)

separate compilation of RTL and testbench

elaboration of the top‑level testbench

batch simulation

interactive waveform viewing

The default top‑level entity is:

Codice
tb_parser
The default waveform format is:

Codice
ghw
Running the Simulation
Full simulation (compile + elaborate + run)
Codice
make all
This performs:

cleanup

RTL compilation

testbench compilation

elaboration

simulation

Waveform output is generated according to the selected format.

Batch simulation only
Codice
make sim
Runs the testbench with:

Codice
ghdl -r tb_parser --wave=wave.ghw --stop-time=200us
(Stop time can be adjusted in the Makefile.)

Interactive simulation + waveform
Codice
make simwave
This target:

removes any previous waveform

runs the simulation with --assert-level=note

opens GTKWave automatically

Useful for debugging.

Waveform Viewing
To manually open GTKWave:

Codice
make wave
or:

Codice
gtkwave wave.ghw &
Debug Logging
Debug messages (severity note) are controlled by:

vhdl
constant ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG : boolean := false;
Defined in:

Codice
cmd_cfg.vhd
Debug OFF (default)
suppresses all debug prints

keeps warning, error, fatal always active

Debug ON
Set:

vhdl
ENABLE_DEBUG_LOG := true;
GHDL supports severity filtering via --assert-level, but the recommended method is to control debug output directly in VHDL.

Cleaning the Directory
To remove generated files:

Codice
make clean
This clears:

workdir/*.o

workdir/*.cf

waveform files

local .o / .cf artifacts

